InboxBankSignalWarn = Point of attention:
InboxBankSignalBad = Alert:
InboxBankSignal_auth_ok = Sender authenticated: the email does come from the domain shown. It does not prove the mailbox was not hacked.
InboxBankSignal_auth_bad = Sender not authenticated: nothing proves this email comes from the domain shown.
InboxBankSignal_imitation = The sender imitates %s.
InboxBankSignal_iban_same = IBAN identical to the one of the card (%s).
InboxBankSignal_iban_differs = IBAN of the email (%s) different from the one of the card (%s). Normal for a real change, but it is exactly what a fraud asks for.
InboxBankSignal_iban_none = No IBAN on the card to compare the one of the email (%s).
InboxBankSignal_iban_nosoc = Sender not attached to a card: the IBAN of the email (%s) cannot be compared with anything.
InboxBankSignal_iban_file = Bank details probably in an attachment (%s): compare the IBAN yourself with the one of the card.
InboxBankSignal_phone_differs = The email gives a number (%s) that is not on your cards. Not necessarily false (new line, switchboard), but do not use it to check.
InboxBankSignal_phone_unknown = The email gives a number (%s) and your cards have none: do not use it to check.
InboxBankSignal_first_time = First time the address %s writes to this mailbox.
InboxBankSignal_reply_to = The answer would go to another address: %s.
InboxBankSignal_pressure = The email hurries or asks for discretion (« %s »): a classic lever of fraud.
InboxBankEvenGreen = Even when everything is green: a mailbox whose password was stolen sends real emails, authenticated, from the real address, often in a real conversation. Only a call to the number you already knew confirms it.
InboxBankWhyTitle = Why so much caution?
InboxBankWhyText = The fraud on bank details is the most costly: a transfer sent to a false account is seldom recovered. The fraudster often reads the hacked mailbox for weeks, knows your exchanges and writes at the right time, just before a payment.
InboxBankStep1 = Do not answer this email to check: the fraudster may be the one who reads the answer.
InboxBankStep2 = Call the person you know, at the number of your Dolibarr card or of a document already received.
InboxBankStep3 = Have the whole IBAN confirmed, digit by digit, aloud.
InboxBankStep4 = For a supplier, have the change approved by a second person before the next payment.
InboxBankStep5 = Write the check below: it stays with the email for your colleagues.
