# Refresh of the lists (1.121.0)
InboxReactivitySetupTitle = Refresh of the lists
InboxReactivitySetupHelp = How soon the changes made by the other users (assignment, tags, flags, moves, new emails) show in the lists. A setting of the server: it applies to every entity.
InboxReactivityMode = Refresh
InboxReactivityStandard = Standard (every 20 seconds)
InboxReactivityFast = Fast (every few seconds)
InboxReactivityInterval = Interval while the user is active (seconds)
InboxReactivityIntervalHelp = Between 3 and 60 seconds.
InboxReactivityIdle = Interval after 2 minutes without activity (seconds)
InboxReactivityIdleHelp = From the active interval up to 300 seconds: the user is probably away from the screen. The full refresh kept as a safety net also slows down, from every minute to every 5 minutes. After 30 minutes without activity the calls stop until the next activity.
InboxReactivityLoadNote = Measured on a development computer: about 2 ms per light call, about 20 ms per full refresh of a list (more with many mailboxes and folders). The full refresh kept as a safety net is counted.
InboxDocTitle_reactivity = Refresh of the lists
InboxDocDesc_reactivity = Fast refresh of the changes made by the other users, and the load it brings
# Instant refresh, push service (1.124.0)
InboxReactivityInstant = Instant (push service)
InboxPushSetupTitle = Push service (instant mode)
InboxPushSetupHelp = Used when the refresh is « Instant ». The service keeps the connections of the browsers open and gives them the changes at once; Dolibarr only sends it a message for each change. It receives numbers only (mailbox, emails, kind of change), never a subject, a text or an address, and gives each user the changes of the mailboxes he can read only. When it does not answer, the lists follow at the rhythm of the fast mode.
InboxPushDriver = Push service
InboxPushDriverHelp = The service that delivers the changes at once: Mercure, or another one added by a module. Its settings show under it; each service keeps its own.
InboxPushDriverDoc = Documentation of the service
InboxPushMercure = Mercure
InboxPushMercureHubUrl = Address of the hub for the browsers
InboxPushMercureHubUrlHelp = Public address ending with /.well-known/mercure, for example https://push.example.com/.well-known/mercure. The browsers of the users connect to it.
InboxPushMercurePublishUrl = Address of the hub for the server
InboxPushMercurePublishUrlHelp = Optional: the address Dolibarr publishes to when it reaches the hub another way (for example http://127.0.0.1:3001/.well-known/mercure). Empty: the address for the browsers.
InboxPushMercureIssuer = Trusted issuer
InboxPushMercureIssuerHelp = Same value as MERCURE_TRUSTED_ISSUERS in the configuration of the hub, for example the address of this Dolibarr (https://erp.example.com). Written in every token as « iss ».
InboxPushMercurePublisherKey = Key of the publishers
InboxPushMercurePublisherKeyHelp = Same value as MERCURE_PUBLISHER_JWT_KEY in the configuration of the hub, at least 32 characters. Kept encrypted and never shown again: leave empty to keep it.
InboxPushMercureSubscriberKey = Key of the subscribers
InboxPushMercureSubscriberKeyHelp = Same value as MERCURE_SUBSCRIBER_JWT_KEY in the configuration of the hub, at least 32 characters, different from the key of the publishers. Kept encrypted and never shown again: leave empty to keep it.
InboxPushBadUrl = %s: an address http or https, without user, password or parameters
InboxPushLastError = Last failure to reach the push service, %s: %s. Meanwhile the lists follow at the rhythm of the fast mode.
InboxPushTest = Test
InboxPushNotConfigured = Fill in the settings of the push service first.
InboxPushTestOk = The push service works: a test event was sent and received back in %s ms.
InboxPushTestSubscribeFailed = The push service refused the subscription (%s): check the address and the key of the subscribers.
InboxPushTestPublishFailed = The push service refused the publication (%s): check the key of the publishers.
InboxPushTestNotReceived = The test event was sent but not received back: check the key of the subscribers in the configuration of the hub.
InboxPushTestPublicUrl = The address for the browsers does not answer as a hub (%s).
